[[00:00:00.380]]
SPEAKER 1
Madam Speaker, I rise to honor the memory of my young constituent, Taylor DeRosa. Taylor made her mark as a student activist at Royal Oak High School. She was beginning her college career at Grand Valley State University when her life was taken so tragically several days

[[00:00:21.100]]
UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKER
ago. I met

[[00:00:22.000]]
SPEAKER 1
Taylor when I was running for Congress in 2018 and she was launching a Students Demand Action chapter. Taylor immediately struck me as a huge splash of sunshine in an unjust world. Her commitment to justice was frank and undeniable. You knew the world would change at least a little bit because Taylor was present, fighting for sensible gun reform, fighting for everyone to see and cherish black lives, fighting to empower women and girls.

[[00:00:55.660]]
UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKER
Taylor

[[00:00:55.720]]
SPEAKER 1
made me feel that every minute we invest in our young people is time well spent. I feel that now, even as we struggle to cope with her loss because she inspired me and so many folks, young and old, all around her. My heart goes out to Taylor's devoted mother, Kara, and all who knew and loved her in this time of heartbreak and mourning. Thank you, Madam Speaker, I yield back.
